In Java 8 we can create threads using lambda expressions because
 Runnable is a functional interface. Instead of creating a separate
 class that implements Runnable, we can directly provide the
  implementation of the run() method using a lambda expression.

  _________________________________________
  3️⃣ What this Lambda Actually Means

  Your code:

  Thread t = new Thread(() -> {
      for(int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
          System.out.println("Hello " + i);
      }
  });


  The lambda:

  () -> { ... }


  is automatically converted into a Runnable implementation.

  So internally JVM treats it like this:

  Runnable r = new Runnable() {
      public void run() {
          for(int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
              System.out.println("Hello " + i);
          }
      }
  };

  Thread t = new Thread(r);

